{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WordNet"},{"text":" is a large lexical database of English where nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs are organized into sets of cognitive synonyms called ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Synsets"}]},{"text":", interlinked by conceptual-semantic and lexical relations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"1. Looking Up Synsets & Definitions","anchor":"1-Looking-Up-Synsets--Definitions","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftNLP","","let wordnet = WordNet.shared","","\/\/ Look up all noun synsets for \"bank\"","let synsets = wordnet.synsets(for: \"bank\", pos: .noun)","for s in synsets {","    print(\"ID: \\(s.id), Definition: \\(s.definition)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"2. Semantic Similarity Metrics","anchor":"2-Semantic-Similarity-Metrics","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftSci implements standard lexical similarity algorithms:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Path Similarity"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Shortest path distance in the hypernym taxonomy:"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Formula:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sim_path(s1, s2) = 1 \/ (1 + distance(s1, s2))","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wu-Palmer Similarity (WUP)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Measures depth of least common subsumer (LCS) relative to synset depths:"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Formula:"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sim_wup(s1, s2) = (2 · depth(LCS)) \/ (depth(s1) + depth(s2))","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let dog = wordnet.synset(\"dog.n.01\")!","let cat = wordnet.synset(\"cat.n.01\")!","","let pathSim = wordnet.pathSimilarity(dog, cat)","let wupSim = wordnet.wuPalmerSimilarity(dog, cat)","","print(\"Path Similarity: \\(pathSim), Wu-Palmer: \\(wupSim)\")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigate semantic relationships, compute synset distances, and explore English hypernym\/hyponym trees."}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"WordNet Semantic Hierarchy & Lexical Graphs","modules":[{"name":"SwiftNLP"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/WordNetAndLexicalGraphs"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"WordNet Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/WordNet","doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/Synset","doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/POS"],"anchor":"WordNet-Types"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftnlp\/wordnetandlexicalgraphs"]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftNLP/documentation/SwiftNLP/Synset":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Synset"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represents a WordNet Synset (Syntactic\/Semantic Set of Synonym Concepts)."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftnlp\/synset","type":"topic","title":"Synset","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/Synset","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Synset"}]},"doc://SwiftNLP/documentation/SwiftNLP":{"role":"c